 4. 🚀 Photo du jour: Caught! 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 SpaceX Starship Ship 42 caught in the arms of the launch tower in Starbase, Texas, as it returned from flight yesterday. Photo: Tim Warner/Getty Images SpaceX caught its next-gen Starship rocket back at its launch pad for the first time yesterday, making rocketry history.

 Why it matters: It's a huge step toward realizing SpaceX's vision of Starship as a fully reusable, 171-foot-tall space launch behemoth. Such reusability could dramatically cut launch costs, potentially ushering in a new era of commercial spaceflight, Axios' Alex Fitzpatrick writes. Go deeper . 

 
 
