 5. 🤒 Measles backslide 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Lindsey Bailey/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The Pan American Health Organization has determined the United States has lost its measles elimination status, Axios' Adriel Bettelheim reports. 

 Why it matters: It's an official recognition of how much the country's public health has deteriorated due to a rolling series of outbreaks since early last year. By the numbers: There have been 5,412 confirmed cases so far this year, compared to 2,289 for all of 2025, according to the CDC's latest tally. 

 Those reports are widely considered to be an undercount, due to the lack of widespread testing and unreported instances of mild illness. Keep reading . 

 
 
